# The Astra screen (D632): result, 2026-11-16

**Run:** six interleaved arm-draws on the 12 seeded topics (`poc/data/clean-astra-screen-2026-11-16/`), with no stop and no charge
above its reserve.
- **Spend:** sol $0.216, astra $1.334, $1.55 in all.
- The first astra request cost $0.079 (uncached); the astra average was $0.037 a send.

**Reading:** 78 blind items read by both families.
- One Codex row on the planted wrong-question control was invalid (Y "n/a" on a theme figure). It was re-asked of a fresh Codex reader
  under the same brief and packet (`reader-codex-packet-2-again-1.jsonl`).
- All six controls then behaved as fixed.

**Verdict under the rule fixed before: promising (a screen; a separate decision follows).**

| | sol | astra |
|---|---:|---:|
| Failed sends of 36 (agreed) | **4** | **1** |
| Failed sends of 36 (strict: unresolved points counted against) | 11 | 9 |
| Model refusals | 18 | 18 |
| Unjustified refusals (agreed) | 4 | 1 |
| Ladders with any agreed or disputed hard-line fault | 0 of 18 | 0 of 18 |
| New-harm topics | | none |

**My hand-read of every send either family failed** (all are refusals; no ladder in either arm drew a hard-line mark):
- **Hugging Face** (week c1/clean-5):
  - sol declined in 2 of 3, both agreed unjustified. The independent audit (`model/rule-audit.md`) also calls this decline unjustified
    on the sources.
  - astra wrote the closing question in 3 of 3, each clean.
- **Memory prices** (week c1/clean-3):
  - sol declined 3 of 3 (2 agreed unjustified, 1 disputed);
  - astra declined 2 of 3 (1 agreed, 1 disputed) and wrote one ladder, unflagged by both families. That ladder defines its own
    aggregation: "the equal-weighted mean of the Q4 2027 versus Q4 2026" change.
  - The audit calls this topic **silent** on the sources.
- **Reflection AI and the equity commitments** (week c1/clean-11 and -13): both models declined 3 of 3. Claude's family fails every
  decline and Codex's holds every one. These are two of the five boundary topics on Alex's page.
- **Supply commitments** (week c1/clean-2): one new astra decline (d1, "total against the cancellable portion"), disputed. I read it as
  unjustified: the description asks the $279 billion total.
- **Robotics venture funding** (fortnight c1/clean-8): astra declined 3 of 3 (no listed theme) and sol wrote 2 ladders. Neither family
  failed either behaviour.

**What it means:**
- On these 12 topics, astra's advantage is the Hugging Face recovery, a sourced unjustified decline that it does not make, plus one
  fewer decline on the silent memory topic.
- On the other boundary topics it declines exactly as sol does. A stronger model does not remove the boundary class (D631); only a
  ruling would.
- **The sample holds none of the topics where ladder faults occurred** (fortnight c1/clean-3, -7, -13; week c1/clean-1, -7). So the
  screen says nothing about astra's ladders where the frozen step and sol wrote faulted ones.

